Client joins zones from the start screen (NAME/ZONE fields, JOIN, Tab focus); two browser clients verified seeing each other. Background tabs throttle rAF, so test pages need bringToFront.                                                                                                   
Zone serves wss (tls_cert/tls_key); head-of-line cost measured: harmless at 40ms RTT, ~1 hitch/1.4s at 150ms+3% loss, bridged by coasting through the shared sim.                                                                                                                              
Clicks were never broken (sub-frame presses are dropped; hold ~90ms in tests), and names are now generated call signs rather than typed.                                                                                                                                                       
Map tiles are typed classes with a variant nibble, and maps load from RLE files the server sends to clients.                                                                                                                                                                                   
Two web-client traps: a stray 'nd' broke every build while 'build.sh | tail -1' hid the exit code, shipping 3 stale bundles (start screen now prints the commit); and Defold resumes audio only from a canvas pointer, so single_file.py unlocks on any gesture.                               
Bombs now splash on wall and direct hits alike (not timeouts, criccomini's call), golden trace regenerated; feed became a notification feed. Client CPU 40%->12% of a core: a Lua buffer-stream write is one C call per float, so vwbuf writes a whole shape per call.                         
No start screen now: land flying, escape opens a menu tree over the live arena, hull change is sim_set_ship_class (a respawn), page draws its own starfield while wasm compiles. A --fragment page needs its own viewport meta or a standalone phone lays out at 980px.                        
Zone hull changes work (C2S_SHIP, core-gated on alive+full bar, upgrades lost); the address field is gone, ZONES only. Weapons are one table model: bounce, proximity, splinter, push and stall all ship as rows, unused by the baseline zone.                                                 
Zones own their rules: settings (with the weapon tables) are packed by the core and sent after the map at join and on reload. Zone files write weapons by name; apply_config rebuilds from the baseline first, so a reload is idempotent and a deleted line reverts.                           
Tech tree: a level is a rung on a per-hull ladder of patterns; an add-on is a transform applied at fire time, per trigger, carried by the shot. Greens carry no type -- the roll happens at pickup over what the hull could ever hold, so every green is takeable.                             
Prize weights are relative and read against the hull's pool; rust corrodes only what a pilot holds, so it never punishes a fresh spawn. Charges are a pattern plus an inventory, with the ready slot in two button bits rather than in sim state.                                              
criccomini's Kinesis Freestyle2 ghosts arrows+space+turn; A/D works, and it is hardware not software. Bounty is derived from what a pilot holds, points are the victim's bounty paid to the finisher, so a fresh spawn is worth nothing.                                                       
Bots hunt by bounty/distance and chase greens when nobody is near, so practice arenas grow real bounties; projectiles retuned faster than any ship (bolt 800 px/s, shell 500, frag 400, burst 600) with lives cut to hold range.                                                               
Tuning comes from ASSS dist/conf/svs, not invention: rounds inherit ship velocity so 2000 vs MaximumSpeed 3250 is deliberate; multifire +50% energy +100% cooldown per rung; prize weights 40 stat / 25 level / 30 multi-shrapnel / 70 charge.                                                 
The original gates almost nothing per ship: charges (3 each), multifire, bouncing bullets, proximity and shrapnel are universal; its whole per-ship diff is nine settings (MaxBombs, ShrapnelMax, BombBounceCount, DoubleBarrel, EmpBomb, CloakStatus, SeeMines, BrickMax, Gravity).           
spawn_prizes (default 30) loads every spawn and flattens the bot skill gap, so calibration pins it to 0. The arena is the full 1024-tile map: a hashed 64-tile cell lattice round the old centre room, meshed by the client in a window round the camera.                                      
